{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1532233-help-with-a-homebrew-chronicle","id":1532233,"title":"Help with a Homebrew Chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-08T00:24:15-08:00","id":1532233,"title":"Help with a Homebrew Chronicle","content":"I'm planning a Contagion Chronicle set during the late Victorian Era, using The Abyss instead of the Contagion. I want to replace the Sworn with new group who use the hidden realm as their Vector, and False be those who use the Abyss as their Vector. But I don't know what kind of ability the Vector should have, what kind of Edge and Specialized ability it should have, and to whome. So I want some suggestion and help with my homebrew.<br /> <br /> <b>Sworn</b><br /> <b>The Theosophical Society</b><br /> <b>What is the Abyss</b>: The Abyss is the Ultimate test, and we must overcome it or else we would all become blind to the truth that the Secret Masters has lay for us.<br /> <b>What we stand to lose</b>: The Truth, all of the thing we learn will become forgotten if we don't handle The Abyss properly.<br /> <b>What we stand to gain</b>: Understanding, so that the world would finally be ready for the teaching of the Secret Masters.<br /> <b>Where we come from</b>: We originate in The Coromandel Coast Indian in 1431, a town was plague by Abyssal Outbreak that suck life from living being, causing them to vivid hallucination before slowly dying. But some people manage to find hidden truth in the maddening hallucination to have enough sense to flee from the area. Since then, The Theosophical Society have always been steadfast in finding hidden truth within World so they may predict where the Abyss would be and what the cure to it might be.<br /> <b>What we do</b>: We study the secret and hidden truth of the world to try and understand their meaning and significant, and teaching people those truth we understand. While keeping the Abyss at bay especially Abyssal Outbreak that affect people mind and perception.<br /> <b>How we organize</b>: We organize ourselve into different <i>sect</i> which usually govern about 3-5 cities and 7 to 10 towns. With each <i>sect</i> putting more focus and important on a single Secret Master teaching than other.<br /> <b>Among the Sworn</b>: The other look to us when they want the information we gather or arcane wisdom we collected. Sometime we come into conflict with SPR over the truth, while their search for knowledge and truth is admirable, their close mindness and ridgrid thinking sometime make them ignorance of the truth, and even labeling the truth as lies.<br /> <b>We get ourselves into trouble when</b>: We put too much focus on finding the hidden truth that we ignore what is right infront of us.<br /> <b>When the Abyss is in remission</b>: We teach all of the knowledge garther, and try to understand the secret we collected, we try to recruit those who have the potential to see the hidden truth and help the community that have been hit by the Abyss.<br /> <b>Vector</b>: Hedge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","user":"Yumlum","date":". 03-08-2024, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T06:07:04-08:00","id":1532236,"title":"","content":"With the focus on the Abyss, it sounds as though it's a Mage chronicle, not a Contagion Chronicle type game with multiple splats. Do you even need vectors at that point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T06:33:48-08:00","id":1532237,"title":"","content":"Well, with the Chronicle I'm planning, mage aren't the only one who is affected by the Abyss, and the Abyss make more thematic sense with the Chronicle I'm planning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T12:10:03-08:00","id":1532249,"title":"","content":"Your <i>Theosophical Society</i> seems to approach their mission as one of discovery, much like the <i>Rosetta Society</i> from the book. The most straightforward thing you could do is to just give them the <i>Semiotics Vector</i> and reflavour it as somehow interacting with or hacking into the Hedge. Your group can see the Hedge as a realm that collects and distorts all information - languages, fairy tales, forgotten secrets, art, internet memes and logical fallacies. As such, a properly trained member could use it to access or subvert knowledge. Not only that, the Hedge would distort Abyssal knowledge making it safer to access for the purpose of the mission.<br /> <br /> You can go a step further and break all Vectors apart, allowing the <i>Theosophical Society</i> to develop any of them that their philosophy could justify. The <i>Breach</i> power from the <i>Realignment Vector</i> would allow entry through Hedge gates,<i> Surveillance</i> from the <i>Authority Vector</i> helps in information gathering and so do multiple powers from the <i>Intel Vector</i>. All are equally appropriate for your group. You can create a mish-mash collection of five powers at different ratings, or just allow characters to develop any number out of order. Reusing official Vectors means that you can also use their printed Edges, so that's extra work averted.<br /> <br /> The same approach can be taken towards the antagonist group. If you want to reflavour a single Vector for their use it likely should be <i>Contagion</i>, but you can mix and match too, depending on their particular philosophy towards the Abyss.<br /> <br /> As for Specializations, you run into the following problem: you can state that Iron Master Werewolves can use <i>Breach</i> to cross mundane barriers, but it's a pointless statement if none of your players choose to play as an Iron Master. The correct answer to your problem is that any Vector has Specializations that fit your players specifically. As for what those Specializations do... ask your players. At some point they will know what they want from the story, and what tweaks do they want for their powers.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T22:48:58-08:00","id":1532274,"title":"","content":"Thank, I will see what official vector could be re-flavor and change to fit better the with The Theosophical Society. But do you have any suggestion for ability that would fit the theme of Theosophical Society and the Hedge?<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <b>Sworn</b><br /> <b><b>S</b></b><b>PR</b> (<b>Society for Paraphysical Research</b>)<br /> <b>What is the </b><b><b>A</b></b><b>byss</b>: The Abyss is an anomaly that we must study, so we can respond to it properly.<br /> <b>What we stand to lose</b>: Our Mind, the nature of the Abyss often twist and bend our mind, causing maddness and obession.<br /> <b>What we stand to gain</b>: Breakthrough, the Abyss is full of possibility, wonder, power waiting to be discover and utilize, think of all the good we could do with all of that.<br /> <b>Where we come from</b>: We originate in The West Midland UK in 1443, in the town of Birmingham, the town was experiencing an Abyssal Outbreak of passion, compelling people to dedicate their life to their magnus opus ignoring everything else. Our founder were those people who magnus opus lead them to discover the Abyss, causing a shift in their passion, their new Magnus Opus is to understand the Abyss, unfortunately their tool and knowledge at the time was too limited for them to achieve their goal. But their afford wasn't wasted as their experiment help close the Abyssal Outbreak.<br /> <b>What we do</b>: We study the Abyss so that we may able to handle it in a way that is most beneficial to humanity, because while the Abyss have a lot of negative effect, it also contain wonder that might help humanity reach it next step.<br /> <b>How we organize</b>: We organize ourselve into different <i>chapter</i> which usually govern about 2-4 cities and 5 to 8 towns. With each <i><i>c</i></i><i>hapter</i> focus on a paticular field of the meta-physic.<br /> <b>Among the Sworn</b>: The other look to us when they want the knowledge of the Abyss or want technical help with the Abyss that the other aren't equip to handle. We sometime come into conflict with The Grand Order of the Immaculate Three, their greed and anger will be their undoing, they pretend to know less than their let on, but what they actually know isn't much either.<br /> <b>We get ourselves into trouble when</b>: Our passion run too deep, we dive into the Abyss trying to find both wonder and horror, but we never expect how those wonder might lure us deeper into the Abyss, or how we can't see the horror that lurk out of our understanding.<br /> <b>When the Abyss is in remission</b>: We try to improve on our research, and repair the tools we use, while we try to make experiment safe and control, sometime accident happen, so we need to recruit new student. Thankfully the new public relation team help us quite a bit with our image.<br /> <b>Vector</b>: Underworld<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","user":"Yumlum","date":". 03-10-2024, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T02:25:58-08:00","id":1532277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1532233-help-with-a-homebrew-chronicle?p=1532274#post1532274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But do you have any suggestion for ability that would fit the theme of Theosophical Society and the Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Breach is the main one. It allows you to enter and leave the Hedge. The following quote from me:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1532233-help-with-a-homebrew-chronicle?p=1532249#post1532249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your group can see the Hedge as a realm that collects and distorts all information - languages, fairy tales, forgotten secrets, art, internet memes and logical fallacies. As such, a properly trained member could use it to access or subvert knowledge. Not only that, the Hedge would distort Abyssal knowledge making it safer to access for the purpose of the mission.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>...was meant to help you figure out how to take pre-existing Vector powers and reflavour them so they are Hedge-related. For example, the first power of <i>Semiotics</i> is <i>Comprehension</i> - it allows you to understand all human languages. You can decide that developing it requires making a deal with the Hedge itself to understand all Hobgoblins, and whenever you want to use it to comprehend human languages you have to think to yourself that Hobgoblins can speak any of them, so the Hedge should oblige you. That sort of thing. Making a Vector Hedge-related requires: developing it in the Hedge, some presence of the Abyss to make reality more malleable, objects from the Hedge, some mental manipulations on the part of the Sworn. \u200b<br /> <br /> I have an extra question for you. Why did you decide to make the Hedge into Theosophical Society's Vector? There's nothing in their history or their mission statement that explains it. Ditto for SPR and Underworld.\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T03:18:31-08:00","id":1532278,"title":"","content":"I decide to have the Hedge be Theosophical Society vector is because they see it as the gateway to where the Secret Master reside. There're a lot of part of Arcadia that are unexplore, and the Theosophical Society belive that the Secret Master are somewhere in those unexplore area. They see the Gentry as another test to prove that you're ready for the master, Changeling within Theosophical Society see their time in Arcadia as the glimsp at the Ultimate Truth, and while they wish to return to Arcadia someday, they wanted to be in their own term, and not resistrict themselve with the one Gentry.<br /> <br /> For SPR, the Underworld answer part of life greatest mystery &quot;what come after death?&quot;, but what come after the ghost pass on? SPR want to investigate that while test out their gadget to see how it would react to ghost numina. There is just so much wonder and horror to be discover within the Underworld, also because of the connection with Mastigo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T03:45:59-07:00","id":1532555,"title":"","content":"<b>Sworn</b><br /> <b>The Grand Order of the Immculate Three</b><br /> <b>What is the </b><b><b>A</b></b><b>byss</b>: The Abyss is the source of pain, we all lost something to Abyss, so we must do everything in our power to stop it.<br /> <b>What we stand to lose</b>: Our Hope, we might have lost something to the Abyss, and for some of us, everything, the only thing that keep us going. If we lose that, we become nothing.<br /> <b>What we stand to gain</b>: Fufillment, the thing that the Immaculate Three want the most, whether it would be power, money, or revenge.<br /> W<b>here we come from</b>: We originate in The Tuscany, Italy in 1470, in the town of Montepulciano, the town was experiencing an Abyssal Outbreak of Emotion, draining people of certain emotion until all of their emotion are gone. The people of the town resort to sinful activity to feel any emltion. Our eternal founder Lady Delvecchio, Millar, and Master Wright, save the town by using their connection to the Shadow and create a large opening in the Gauntlet, releasing the Spirit of Emotion. But they pay the price for their power with a little bit of themselve. Lady Delvecchio lost her physical sight, but can see what is hidden to the naked eye, Millar lost the ability to feel sadness but can get what you want, Master Wright lost his voice but can silence other people.<br /> <b>What we do</b>: We battle against the Abyss to stop the pain, we use everything in our power not only to just fix the Abyssal Outbreak but to destroy or at least damage the Abyss enough that it can't break into the World anymore. We do that by expanding our business empire, doing favor for people in power, and making deal in the Shadow.<br /> <b>How we organize</b>: We organize ourselve into different <i>house</i> which usually govern about 1-3 cities and 4 to 6 towns. With each <i>house</i> focus on a paticular way of the spiritualism.<br /> <b>Among the Sworn</b>: The other look to us when they want resources, hire mercenaries, or power from beyond. We sometime come into conflict with The Hellfire Company, their blasphemous ritual, and sinful activity were the very reason that we were founded.<br /> <b>We get ourselves into trouble when</b>: We focus too much on our personal goal than the Abyss, we shift too many of our resouce to our own end instead of helping other.<br /> <b>When the Abyss is in remission</b>: We speard the word about Spiritualism and try to take down those who oppose our ideology, we try to expand our influence in the business world, underworld, and the unseen world.<br /> <b>Vector</b>: Shadow<br /> <br /> <b>The Hellfire Company</b><br /> <b>What is the </b><b><b>A</b></b><b>byss</b>: The Abyss is the great cleansing, the end of time is near, and it mission is to rid the world of all it impurity before the world can be reborn.<br /> <b>What we stand to lose</b>: Our Integrity, we are the darkness that needed for the world to be in Balance, but dealing with the Abyss can cause us to stop maintaining the balance and start to become monsters without a purpose.<br /> <b>What we stand to gain</b>: Balance, the world is out of balance with the Abyss creeping more and more into the world, we must absorb the taint of the world, until the world become balance once again.<br /> W<b>here we come from</b>: We originate in North-Central Morocco in 1483, the entire region was suffering from Abyssal Outbreak of Humanity, people start to behave weirdly, people feature start to shift becoming more predatory. The Abyss would have spread into other region and turn Morocco into the land of Monster if not for our us, we saw what people became, and what we were becoming. So we embrance our monstrosity to protect other from the same fate, which lead us to the source of the Outbreak, we manage to cure the Outbreak, but lose some of our member to monstrosity.<br /> <b>What we do</b>: We use the Darkness against the Abyss, seeking eldritch knowledge knowledge and using blasphemous ritual, we seek to not stop the Abyss, but to make sure that the Abyss don't unbalance the scale.<br /> <b>How we organize</b>: We organize ourselve into different <i>division</i> which usually govern about 1-2 cities and 3 to 4 towns. With each <i>division</i> focus on a paticular vice.<br /> <b>Among the Sworn</b>: The other look to us when they need a job done that no one else wanted to do, or they want information about the darkness of the world. We sometime get into conflict with The Heavenly Order, they confuse truth with zeal, and kill the darkness that is necessary to maintain the world.<br /> <b>We get ourselves into trouble when</b>: We focus too much on the darkness that we forget to protect the light, a world without light is as bad as a world without darkness.<br /> <b>When the Abyss is in remission</b>: We step into the light, and foster it to prepare for the next time the Abyss come, we hunt down the darkness that don't keep themselve in check, and help community bond.<br /> <b>Vector</b>: Inferno<br /> <br /> <b>The Heavenly Order</b><br /> <b>What is the Abyss</b>: The Abyss is the punishment of the gods, humanity are far from pure, but as age pass humanity start to convice themselve with the lie that we are superior than anything else on earth, so the heaven punish humanity hubris twisting our creation against us.<br /> <b>What we stand to lose</b>: Order, we might look to be unify but having a global organization with different conflicting faith working together isn't easy, and with the Abyss it a miracle we even exist, if we lose order the Abyss would spread quicker and more wildly.<br /> <b>What we stand to gain</b>: Reformation, we don't need humanity to become pure, but we want humanity to stop creating taint and clean up the mess that they make.<br /> <b>Where we come from</b>: We originate in Guangzhou, China in 1559, the town was experiencing an Abyssal Outbreak of Plague, it would speard to the entire region if not for our swift and percise action, we manage to cure those who only got the Abyss recently and kill anyone else. It's might seem extreme but order need to be upheld.<br /> <b>What we do</b>: We root out the taint, we try to redeem those who are affected by it, but sometime you must cut down a limp to save your body.<br /> <b>How we organize</b>: We organize ourselve into different <i>legion</i> which usually govern about 1 city and 2 towns. With each <i>legion</i> focus on a oath.<br /> <b>Among the Sworn</b>: The other look to us when they want the best warrior, or strategist. We sometime come into conflict with The Theosophical Society, while they mix faith is similair to us, they pratice of seeking the hidden truth is backward.<br /> <b>We get ourselves into trouble when</b>: We maybe a bit zealous with Abyss, and destroy more than we manage to protect.<br /> <b>When the Abyss is in remission</b>: We maintain our goal in secret, promoting order and root out taint wherever we see.<br /> <b>Vector</b>: Empyrean","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}